      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\n- **Dose ordered:** 4250 mg three times daily is 12,750 mg/day.\n- **Maximum dose:** The usual maximum for metformin is 2,550 mg/day (about 850 mg three times daily). Immediate-release tablets are typically given as 500 mg or 850 mg per dose.\n- **Risk:** This is about 5 times the maximum. It carries a serious risk of lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nThis may be a typo, for example 425 mg or 850 mg per dose. Can you confirm the intended dose?\n\nCommon regimens are:\n- 500 mg PO twice daily with meals, which is a typical starting dose.\n- 850 mg PO three times daily with meals, which is the usual maximum.\n\nOnce you confirm the dose, ideally after checking with your resident or attending, I'll enter the order right away."
      }
